{
  "name": "JH VC (NAM)",
  "notes": "Late-60s wah-fuzz blues-rock: wah -> Fuzz Face -> cranked 60s Marshall Super Lead. The pedal-controlled wah is not mapped yet, so the intro uses TOUCH WAH (Mu-Tron style auto-wah, opens with picking strength). Wah sits in the EFX slot; the MOD slot hosts the fuzz (as EFX) and is moved BEFORE the amp, so the order is wah -> fuzz -> amp like the original rig. Amp = 1968 Super Lead NAM in slot 5 (TONE3000 '1968 Marshall Super Lead 12 000 Series Drive A2', AmalgamAudio, full rig: IR off), MASTER kept low because NAM + fuzz is loud. Strat neck/middle, Eb tuning. SCN1 rhythm (main riff), SCN2 solo, SCN3 intro (muted wah scratching).",
